        <h2>Why So Many Kids' Apps Fail in Airplane Mode</h2>
        <p>
          To keep initial download sizes small, many large subscription apps act like streaming services: the home screen loads, but each mini-game or video is fetched from the cloud only when your child taps it. Worse still, some subscription apps periodically require an active Wi-Fi connection just to verify that your monthly billing is still active!
        </p>
        <p>
          For stress-free family travel—whether on a long-haul airplane flight, a train ride, a mountain road trip without cell service, or a quiet restaurant wait—look for apps that store <strong>all assets locally on your device</strong> and feature <strong>calm audio</strong> that works well with or without headphones.
